OCDM: do not clean up twice when the plug-in cannot start

Initialize() calls Deinitialize() itself when it fails, which releases the
service and sets it to null. Thunder (R4.4) then calls Deinitialize() once
more for the failed activation, and that second call uses the null service:
the whole framework ends with a segmentation fault. Seen on tv-emu, where the
implementation could not be instantiated; any failure of Initialize() does it.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet offered to rdkcentral/entservices-opencdmi]

diff --git a/plugin/OCDM.cpp b/plugin/OCDM.cpp
index dd29c5b..d10545c 100644
--- a/plugin/OCDM.cpp
+++ b/plugin/OCDM.cpp
@@ -157,6 +157,13 @@ namespace Plugin {
 
     /*virtual*/ void OCDM::Deinitialize(PluginHost::IShell* service)
     {
+        if (_service == nullptr) {
+            // Initialize() failed and has cleaned up already, by calling this
+            // itself. The framework calls it once more when an activation
+            // fails: there is nothing left to release.
+            return;
+        }
+
         ASSERT(_service == service);
 
         _service->Unregister(&_notification);
